### 4.5 Electron Identification

Electrons can provide a very clean probe of early conditions and the evolution of the collision environment as they do not strongly interact with the medium. The TPC has been used as the primary tool for electron identification in STAR, and utilizes the reconstructed momentum and ionization energy loss per unit length (d\(E\)/d\(x\)). The TOF and BEMC have been used to further discriminate between electrons and

